---
/* THE PAGE THE FRONT PAGE COULD NOT BE.
 *
 * This material used to sit under the map as eight cards, each with a
 * paragraph and a list of spellings. It was cut to a single strip because
 * below a map it read as documentation of somebody else's research — half a
 * screen about families the reader has no connection to, in the place where
 * they were trying to find their own.
 *
 * The fault was the position, not the writing. A reader who has clicked
 * «My Work» is asking exactly the question the long version answers. So the
 * long version lives here, and the front page keeps the map.
 *
 * EVERY EXAMPLE ON THIS PAGE IS A REAL ARCHIVE, read from the same file the
 * strip used. Nothing here is illustrative.
 */
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { u } from "../lib/url.js";
import showcase from "../data/archives-showcase.json";
import regions from "../../public/regions.json";

const kids = {
  id: "our-family",
  name: "Our Family",
  url: "https://daviddef.github.io/Our-Family/",
  accent: "var(--accent)",
  where: "written for children",
  what: "The landing site the eight archives meet in, written so that a "
      + "six-year-old can follow their own family back — which is the thing "
      + "people actually want, and the thing a list of parish registers does "
      + "not convey.",
};
const all = [kids, ...showcase.archives];
const names = [...new Set(showcase.archives.flatMap((a) => a.names || []))];
const eras = regions.regions.reduce((a, r) => a + r.eras.length, 0);
---
<Base
  title="My Work"
  eyebrow={`${all.length} family archives · ${names.length} surnames followed`}
  dek="Family histories where every claim carries its record, and the whole thing is a site a family can walk through.">

  <div class="k-bar"><h2>How it is done</h2></div>
  <ul class="k-grid mw-how">
    <li class="k-card"><span class="k-ico" aria-hidden="true">🏛</span><h3>An archive, not a tree</h3>
      <p>A tree says <em>Giovanni was born in 1861</em>. An archive says which register, book and folio, and how sure that makes it. The first is a position, the second an argument someone can check.</p></li>
    <li class="k-card"><span class="k-ico" aria-hidden="true">📍</span><h3>Start from the ground</h3>
      <p>Surnames move and mutate; ground does not. Each archive is anchored on a place first (Arienzo, Senj, Piedimonte Etneo, Schubin) and the people hang off it.</p></li>
    <li class="k-card"><span class="k-ico" aria-hidden="true">🗺</span><h3>Whose archive was it?</h3>
      <p>A 1930 baptism in a Croatian village is filed under <em>Italy</em>, because the village was Italian then. The atlas carries {eras} eras across {regions.regions.length} regions for this: <a href={u("/providers/#regions")}>whose archive held this ground, and when</a>.</p></li>
    <li class="k-card"><span class="k-ico" aria-hidden="true">🧪</span><h3>Test the family stories</h3>
      <p>Some are true, some half true, and the wrong half usually points at the record. The Lerena archive tests four traditions against the record, one at a time.</p></li>
    <li class="k-card"><span class="k-ico" aria-hidden="true">📝</span><h3>Write down what you did not find</h3>
      <p>A search that returned nothing is a result. Every archive records its negative searches so nobody repeats them.</p></li>
    <li class="k-card"><span class="k-ico" aria-hidden="true">⚖️</span><h3>Grade every claim</h3>
      <p>Proven, probable, a candidate, or a family story, and it says which. A candidate quietly promoted to fact is how a wrong ancestor gets inherited.</p></li>
  </ul>

  <div class="k-bar"><h2>{all.length} archives, each with its own wall</h2><span class="k-count">four continents</span></div>
  <ul class="k-grid mw-works">
    {all.map((a) => (
      <li>
        <a href={a.url} class="k-card is-link">
          <h3>{a.name}</h3>
          <p class="mw-where">{a.where}</p>
          <p>{a.what}</p>
          {a.names && a.names.length > 1 && (
            <span class="k-pills">{a.names.map((n) => <span class="k-pill is-plain">{n}</span>)}</span>
          )}
        </a>
      </li>
    ))}
  </ul>

  <div class="k-bar"><h2>Why this atlas exists</h2></div>
  <div class="k-prose">
    <p>Eight of those archives hit the same three geographic walls: the place had changed its name, the border had moved so the records sat in another country's archive, and "online" meant four or five different things. <a href={u("/")}>Record Atlas</a> is that part of the work, taken out and pointed at the world. The family facts stayed in the archives; what came out was the geography.</p>
    <p>Know a record set this map is missing? <a href={u("/add/")}>Add a source</a>. It is the most useful thing a stranger can do for it, and it costs nothing.</p>
  </div>
</Base>

<style is:global>
  .mw-how .k-card .k-ico { margin-bottom: 4px; }
  .mw-works { grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(min(100%, 300px), 1fr)); }
  .mw-works > li { display: flex; }
  .mw-works .k-card { flex: 1; }
  .mw-where { font: 600 11px/1.3 var(--mono); letter-spacing: .06em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--ink-3) !important; }
  .mw-works .k-pills { margin-top: 6px; gap: 6px; }
  .mw-works .k-pill { font-size: 12px; padding: 3px 9px; }
</style>
